speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, provision is made for the appeal in Section 31(2) which reads;
An appeal to the Appeal Tribunal shall be instituted by filing with the Tribunal a notice in writing in a form prescribed by the rules made pursuant to subsection 27(2).
Those rules have not been promulgated in any way. Will the minister now tell the House what is the nature of the notice in writing and the form prescribed by the rules that has to be followed in order to make an appeal or is the minister unaware of the form?
